+# DOT appointment-file containers and the FAA follow-up trail
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · B129 / PD01–PD05
+
+NARA's public catalog export identifies **Box 5 of LTI-0398-2019-0006** with the catalog boundary **IG Agendas**. It also identifies two appointment-file containers whose listed dates cover the **August 31, 2006** FAA referral report, and lists **120 file-unit descriptions** under Deputy Secretary Maria Cino's appointment series. These records narrow the search to specific boxes and folders. The actual agendas, folder contents, corrected answer and FAA decision remain unacquired. [Box 5 series, NAID 230671051](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/230671051) · [Preserved official export object, line 16](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-152.jsonl) · [FAA referral memorandum](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=1)
+
+## Most specific retrieval locations
+
+| Catalog record | What the description identifies |
+| --- | --- |
+| **NAID 230671051**, **LTI-0398-2019-0006**, **UD-19D 3** | Appointment Files of the Deputy Secretary and Secretary. The description covers briefings, schedules, reports, correspondence and drafts. The exact Box 5 boundary is `Box 5: Amtrak Board 11/04  #2 THRU IG Agendas`. The title gives a direct lead to the IG agendas. Contents, dates and whether any agenda concerns this case remain unverified. The catalog marks the series **Restricted - Partly**. The public FY 2019 Q4 notice calls its seven containers **possibly restricted**. [Catalog description, line 16](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-152.jsonl) · [FY 2019 Q4 notice](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2019-quarter-4#:~:text=LTI-0398-2019-0006) |
+| **NAID 295824641**, **LTI-0398-2021-0015**, **UD-23D 1**, **HS1-793332560** | Appointment Files of Deputy Secretary Maria Cino. It says files are arranged by meeting or event date and lists meeting and briefing materials. **Container 4** is bounded by **June 27, 2006** and **November 21, 2006** titles. **Container 5** starts with the **November 22, 2006 Performance & Accountability Report FY 2006** title. The series identifies a folder list at the reference unit. The published file-unit descriptions add specific targets below. [Series record, line 16](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-151.jsonl) |
+| **NAID 225277157**, **LTI-0398-2019-0003**, **UD-19D 1** | The catalog calls this *Appointment Files of Secretary Norman Mineta and Acting Secretary Maria Cino*. It describes daily briefing files. **Container 1** covers **June 11, 2002–November 11, 2003** and **Container 11** covers **August 14, 2006–November 30, 2006**. Both are item-search windows. [Catalog series record, line 24](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-3.jsonl) |
+| **NAID 296773939**, **UD-23D 3 Container 1** | The Peters appointment series lists briefing materials and meeting notes. The specific container's boundary is **October 4, 2006–December 15, 2006**. This includes the **December 12** case closure date recorded by OIG. Catalog metadata records three accession IDs in the series, with the container listed under its entry number. No case entry or crosswalk to a particular workflow was found. [Catalog series record, line 21](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-308.jsonl) · [Earlier closure record review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/CONFLICTS.md) |
+
+The catalog separately identifies **NAID 226413945 / LTI-0398-2019-0001** as official DOT board and committee reports and minutes maintained by the Executive Secretariat, arranged alphabetically by committee name. Its reported end date is **December 31, 2003**. It provides a May 2003-era lead alongside a boundary that excludes the 2006 dates. [Committee Files, line 21](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-239.jsonl)
+
+## File units to check
+
+The Cino series has 120 linked file-unit descriptions in the export. Eight were checked against their exact JSONL records. Among the most relevant are the **October 6, 2006 Scheduling Process** file, **October 20, 2006 FAA MAC Meeting**, **November 1 Policy Goals & Priorities**, **November 22 Performance & Accountability Report FY 2006**, and **December 20 National Strategy for Aviation Security**. A **November 30, 2005 OIG Semiannual Report** folder is an earlier example of OIG material described in the same series. The folder titles identify records to inspect. The eight selected records have zero digital objects in the export. [Scheduling Process, NAID 608696677](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/608696677) · [FAA MAC Meeting, NAID 608696679](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/608696679) · [Performance & Accountability, NAID 608696696](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/608696696) · [All eight source locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Conflicting descriptions retained
+
+- The FY 2023 accession workbook gives **TR-0398-2021-0015**, **5 container(s)** and **April 12, 2005–December 18, 2007**. Catalog NAID 295824641 gives **LTI-0398-2021-0015** and the same dates. It labels containers **1–5** but its measurement field gives **4.0 FRC Carton, Standard** and its extent field gives **4 linear feet**. Keep the identifiers, carton count, container labels and linear extent separate. The matching numeric part, title subject and dates support a candidate link. The transfer and location records are needed to confirm it. [FY 2023 workbook, Sheet1 row 813](https://www.archives.gov/files/new-accessions/fy-23-accessions.xls) · [Catalog series record](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-151.jsonl)
+- The FY 2019 Q3 notice titles **LTI-0398-2019-0003** for **Norman Mineta and Mary Peters**. The catalog title for the same accession names **Norman Mineta and Acting Secretary Maria Cino**. Both give **June 11, 2002–November 30, 2006**. Preserve both titles and seek the transfer and box paperwork before assigning folder coverage. [FY 2019 Q3 notice](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2019-quarter-3#:~:text=LTI-0398-2019-0003) · [Catalog series record](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-3.jsonl)
+- The FY 2019 Q4 notice gives **January 1, 1996–December 31, 2007** for **LTI-0398-2019-0006**. The catalog series gives **March 18, 2004–December 31, 2007**. The two descriptions do not supply a box-level start-date crosswalk. [FY 2019 Q4 notice](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2019-quarter-4#:~:text=LTI-0398-2019-0006) · [Catalog series record](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-152.jsonl)
+- The export's RG 398 parent description **NAID 696** gives **1958–2005**. The Cino and Peters series have later end dates. Keep each field with its own record level. A search restricted to the parent end date would miss both series. [Record group, line 2](https://nara-national-archives-catalog.s3.amazonaws.com/descriptions/record-groups/rg_398/rg_398-26.jsonl)
+
+## Test scope and next records
+
+The public S3 listing for the documented RG 398 prefix returned **400 objects** and **IsTruncated=false**. Their **84,971,277 bytes** yielded **8,294 descriptions** with no duplicate NAID in the acquired set. All objects matched the manifest length, ETag and last-modified fields. SHA-256 was calculated and the saved objects reread. The follow-up searched full JSON lines for the case report number, investigation number and specific phrases and accessions listed in the ledger. Its two hits were the Cino accession and the Box 5 `IG Agendas` boundary. No exact case-key match was found. The targeted ancestry test located the 120 Cino file-unit records. It yielded zero descendant descriptions for the other five selected series in this snapshot. Those results describe the export and tested keys. They leave actual folder contents and the live catalog's coverage open. [NARA dataset guide](https://www.archives.gov/developer/national-archives-catalog-dataset) · [Manifest, checks and record hashes](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+- [ ] **PD02–PD04.** Locate **Box 5 / UD-19D 3 / LTI-0398-2019-0006** folder inventory and the actual **IG Agendas**. Check dates, routing, case references and action-item follow-through.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD04.** Inspect the candidate Cino and Peters containers and date-specific file units for the original agency briefing, tasking, action/no-action decision or recommendation tracking. Keep the Mineta/Cino title, Mineta/Peters notice and physical container labels with their separate provenance.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD05.** The corrected May 2003 answer and dated receipt, signed disposition, recommendation outcomes and House 3550 cover and enclosure remain open. [Existing case-specific queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/OPEN-RECORDS.md)
